# .NET build output.
#
# Scoped here rather than added to the repository root .gitignore on purpose: that file
# belongs to main, and this branch's rule is to stay additive so merges from main keep
# being trivial (see docs/dotnet-migration/README.md). A new file in a new directory
# cannot conflict; an edit to the root ignore list can.
#
# Only the .NET artifacts need listing; the root .gitignore covers the rest.

bin/
obj/

# Two root rules catch .NET folders by accident, so they are re-included here:
#  - "build/" (a build folder anywhere) also matches dotnet/build/, the shared MSBuild props and targets;
#  - "*.app" (a macOS app bundle) also matches TmDq.App/, because git on Windows ignores case.
# Without these lines git status does not even list them, and a commit silently leaves them out.
!build/
!TmDq.App/
